    rdfs:comment "0.40.0 (2026-10-15): Mastering Bitcoin 3rd edition, chapter 10: Bitcoin Network planned into Iter_6 before any work on it: planning, refinement, score, build and verify tasks per story, the stories Ready. Nothing started or Done in this version."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "0.39.0 (2026-10-15): Recorded Done through the evidence bridge (chapter check exit 0 and every cited file's SHA-256 verified, dependencies Done): ST_Research_Ch09. Open after the run: none. The open scores of the planned chapter were re-run, unchanged (none). Second readings of the second lineage's objectives written."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "0.38.0 (2026-10-15): Recorded Done through the evidence bridge (chapter check exit 0 and every cited file's SHA-256 verified, dependencies Done): ST_Research_Ch08. Open after the run: none. The open scores of the planned chapter were re-run, unchanged (Score_Deck_Ch08, Score_Deck_Ch09, Score_Page_Ch08, Score_Page_Ch09, Score_Research_Ch09). Second readings of the second lineage's objectives written."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "0.37.0 (2026-10-15): Work on ST_Research_Ch09 begun (the story and its build task InProgress, started 2026-10-15T01:39:29 UTC) after the start gate said READY for it. Nothing else started, nothing Done."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "0.36.0 (2026-10-15): Work on ST_Research_Ch08 begun (the story and its build task InProgress, started 2026-10-15T01:39:02 UTC) after the start gate said READY for it. Nothing else started, nothing Done."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "0.35.0 (2026-10-15): Mastering Bitcoin 3rd edition, chapter 9: Transaction Fees planned into Iter_5 before any work on it: planning, refinement, score, build and verify tasks per story, the stories Ready. Nothing started or Done in this version."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "0.34.0 (2026-10-15): Recorded Done through the evidence bridge (chapter check exit 0 and every cited file's SHA-256 verified, dependencies Done): ST_Deck_Ch05, ST_Research_Ch05, ST_Page_Ch05, ST_Deck_Ch06, ST_Research_Ch06, ST_Deck_Ch07, ST_Research_Ch07, ST_Page_Ch07. Open after the run: ST_Page_Ch06. The open scores of the planned chapter were re-run, unchanged (Score_Deck_Ch08, Score_Page_Ch08, Score_Research_Ch08). Second readings of the second lineage's objectives written."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "0.33.0 (2026-10-14): The build and verify tasks of chapter 8 moved from the first lineage's Backlog container into the second lineage's Iter_4, which version 0.32.0 had left them out of; version 0.32.0 did not validate (L1). No other change."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "0.32.0 (2026-10-14): Mastering Bitcoin 3rd edition, chapter 8: Signatures planned into Iter_4 before any work on it: planning, refinement, score, build and verify tasks per story, the stories Ready. Nothing started or Done in this version."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "0.31.0 (2026-10-14): first readings of the second lineage's objectives: admitted Done 0 of 9, evidence verified 0, dates from git 0, cited files changed 0; chapters 8-14 Done: decks 0, research 0, pages 0."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "0.30.0 (2026-10-14): closedAtCommit of the Backlog stage output of the second lineage set to the commit that closed it."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "0.29.0 (2026-10-14): second lineage, Backlog stage closed: the first lineage's out-scoped work is admitted (0 admitted stories of chapters 5-7 recorded Done with bridge-verified evidence; admitted still open: ST_Deck_Ch05, ST_Research_Ch05, ST_Page_Ch05, ST_Deck_Ch06, ST_Research_Ch06, ST_Page_Ch06, ST_Deck_Ch07, ST_Research_Ch07, ST_Page_Ch07; chapters 8-14 admitted open, to be planned; the three epics and the initiative carried unchanged). Chapter checks that FAILED when the bridge ran them: ST_Deck_Ch05, ST_Research_Ch05, ST_Research_Ch06, ST_Page_Ch06, ST_Research_Ch07. Chapter checks that passed but whose story stays open because the research it depends on is not Done: ST_Page_Ch05, ST_Deck_Ch06, ST_Deck_Ch07, ST_Page_Ch07."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "0.28.0 (2026-10-14): second lineage, Objective stage closed."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "0.27.0 (2026-10-14): second lineage, Goal stage closed."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "0.26.0 (2026-10-14): second lineage, Scope stage closed (admit the finished chapters 5-7; build chapters 8-14)."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "0.25.0 (2026-10-14): second lineage opened under the same Mission (Mission stage closed; the Mission is continued unchanged - its re-affirmation is the owner's act, G14, not performed here)."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "0.24.0 (2026-10-14): the lineage is Achieved on its finished scope; the succession ex:Succession_Ch05_14 under the same mission opens the successor lineage ex:Lineage2 and resolves the out-scoping declaration."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "0.23.0 (2026-10-14): the lineage's unfinished work is out-scoped by an owner-rule PartialScopeDeclaration (30 stories of chapters 5-14, three epics, one initiative); the root container's asserted state is dropped because the rules derive it."@en .

ex:Lineage a backlog:Lineage ;
    rdfs:label "First lineage run for the SEN0401 decks"@en ;
    backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission ; backlog:lineageOrdinal 1 ; backlog:lineageArchived false ;
    backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_Achieved ;
    backlog:adoptsObligationSet backlog:OS_SDLC_v2 ; backlog:adoptionRecordedAtOpen true .

ex:Mission a backlog:Mission ;
    rdfs:label "Teach SEN0401 from the edition students can now read for free"@en ;
    backlog:missionFor ex:Backlog ;
    backlog:hasMissionStatement "Every SEN0401 lecture teaches what the third edition of Mastering Bitcoin teaches, chapter by chapter, with a deck, the research behind it and an interactive page - renewed from the book and researched evidence, within the term theme of semantic technologies." ;
    backlog:hasMissionOrigin "Owner rulings of 2026-09-24 and 2026-09-25: the course outline was updated to the third edition of Mastering Bitcoin (Antonopoulos and Harding, O'Reilly, December 2023, CC BY-SA 4.0) and its fourteen chapters; the term theme is semantic technologies; and on 2026-09-25 at 01:15 Istanbul time the owner made SEN0401's first chapter the most urgent work, ahead of SEN0414's second, because SEN0401 teaches at 09:00 that morning. Measured before this mission was written: the SEN0401 repository was created empty on 2026-09-24 and holds nothing; the book's source, tag third_edition_print1, lists fourteen chapters." ;
    backlog:hasMissionOutcome "A student in SEN0401 finds, for each chapter, a deck, an interactive page and the sources behind them, grounded in the edition they can read for free." ;
    backlog:outcomeRationale "The course was being taught from a second-edition outline whose chapter structure the third edition changed: Signatures and Transaction Fees are new chapters, and the old scripting chapter became Authorization and Authentication. Renewing chapter by chapter against the source is the only way to teach what students actually read." ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:producedByStage ex:Out_Mission ;
    backlog:missionSource "Mastering Bitcoin, 3rd edition, from the authors' own repository at tag third_edition_print1 (github.com/bitcoinbook/bitcoinbook); research by RDODI's four-stage procedure v1.6.0 with its pedagogy stage; structured by CME's course profile." .

ex:Area_Deck a backlog:ScopeArea ;
