ex:ST_Page_Ch13 backlog:hasAuditNote "Dated note, 2026-10-16 (agent-reported by the course coordinator, not re-verified here): the chapter 13 page is built (commit 0937e8c, version 9.48.0) but FAILS one check in both page tests 9.34.0 and 9.35.0: 'code questions change the chapter's numbers on the fly' (0 varied questions; 4 of 35 examples are variable). Result: 366 passed, 2 skipped, 1 failed. The story is NOT recorded Done and stays InProgress. The page agent is looking for a legitimate fix; no gate was weakened." .
ex:ST_Page_Ch12 backlog:hasAuditNote "Dated note, 2026-10-16 (agent-reported by the course coordinator, not re-verified here; the Done record is untouched): the committed chapter 12 page (commit 97bd35a) carries a book code listing under CC BY-SA 4.0 with no separate code licence found. This is an open licence question. A rebuild is in progress; when it is committed and passes the chapter check it will be recorded as new evidence." .

ex:ST_Page_Ch13 backlog:hasAuditNote "Dated note, 2026-10-16 (agent-reported by the course coordinator, not re-verified here): the page agent found no honest fix for the failing check 'code questions change the chapter's numbers on the fly'. The check calls the question maker once per concept in a seeded order, and only 5 of 35 examples have an editable number. Making the maker refuse code questions for non-editable examples would be gaming the test, so it was not done. No gate was weakened. The story stays open (InProgress, not Done) pending a ruling on whether chapters whose examples read recorded runs are held to that check; that is a test-design question, not a page defect that this register can settle." .

