    backlog:hasAuditNote "All page checks ran against a copy of the page carrying a TEST release key: they prove the page logic, not the instructor's real key. The page of chapter 13 FAILS its one check (as before) and is admitted failing, with its file hash only. The page of chapter 8 fails page test 9.34.0 (a crash after the question-type check; no honest fix found, agent-reported) and passes the newest test, 9.35.0, with 3 skips, which is the test the recorded check runs. The page of chapter 3 is v9.66.0 on template 9.50.0 and supersedes two earlier commits; the first bridge run of chapter 1 failed the load-time budget while other checks ran in parallel and passed when run alone. Agent-reported, not verified from here: 403 or a bot challenge for the CNBC and CoinGecko links (chapter 1), the NYT and learnmeabitcoin HD-wallets links (chapter 5), the learnmeabitcoin Transaction link (chapter 6) and the Schnorr 1991 article (chapter 8), so those links were not verifiable by the builders; archive.org copies were used for hashcash, b-money, the bitcoinfoundation 2014 post and the Spilman reply, and raw.githubusercontent.com for GitHub files; Wikipedia stays for the Mt. Gox card (chapter 13) and the Lightning Network, Trezor and Casascius wiki cards (chapter 14); the agent that rebuilt chapters 8 to 14 edited the committed sen0401_links_v1_0_0.py (the Hashcash entry) after its commit, which breaks the no-edit rule; corrected on the way: the chapter 2 slide 12 linked bitcointalk topic 141 (wrong) and now links topic 183, and the chapter 3 slide 6 date changed from 9 January to 8 January 2009 after Satoshi's post header (Thu Jan 8 14:27:40 EST 2009), \"Six days\" became \"Five days\"; the older chapter 3 pages and the materials register sen0401_materials_v1_4_* still say 9 January (open). Dates: first and last git commit of the listed rebuild commits (page rebuilds); the commits are 20f2ea2, 740cf3f, c3a12d1, 12f5941, c161485, 126215a, b13ad1f, 600c337, b09e22d, a401f89, 330d09a, a534ba3, 58b1a30, 8c02ca6." .
