ex:Revision_Lineage3_Objective a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Objective stage: the class model is paid"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Objective ;
    backlog:revisionReason "The Backlog stage of the third lineage owes a class model of the domain at the analysis level (Ob_Backlog_ClassDiagram, required). The course session closed that stage on 2026-10-18 (register version 0.101) with a waiver of the obligation instead of meeting it, and dropped the data concern from the two link-pass stories because that concern in turn owes a design-level class model. That was an ERROR of the course session, not a gap of the framework: a requirement of the lineage was bypassed, and it should have been met in the stage that owes it, in the same commit. The owner's instruction of 2026-10-19: \"If there is a requirement in the lineage you should never bypass it. This is a drift and breaking the rules. You should never do such a thing. And you should do this in time not after the completion of the work.\" This revision pays the debt: the Objective stage is rebuilt with the analysis-level class model and the design-level class model (the Mission, Scope and Goal outputs stand), the data concern is restored on the two stories, and the Backlog stage is rebuilt after it, re-admitting the same items by admission and not re-dating them, with no waiver. The earlier outputs and the waiver stay in the register, readable as the dated record of the error. The revision is recorded as decided by the builder role: the owner gave the instruction above, but did not himself decide this revision, and his confirmation of it is listed as open." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_Objective, ex:Out3_Backlog ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "1587e48" .
ex:Out3_Objective backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_Backlog backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_Backlog rdfs:comment "ERROR of the course session, recorded 2026-10-19: this output was closed on 2026-10-18 with a waiver of the required class-model obligation of the Backlog stage. A requirement of the lineage was bypassed; it should have been met in time. This output and the Objective output are retracted by the stage revision ex:Revision_Lineage3_Objective and rebuilt with the model; the waiver on this output stays as the dated record of the error and is not relied on by the rebuilt output."@en .

ex:Model3_Class a backlog:ModelArtifact ; rdfs:label "How a link-pass story and its evidence are stored"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ClassDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ;
    backlog:declaresState "A Story (the deck link pass or the page link pass) is admitted by the Backlog output of this lineage as a pre-lineage item. It has a start and a finish from git, one TestHarness, one TestEvidence per chapter whose check passed and one ArtifactEvidence per cited file (path and SHA-256). A chapter whose check fails has the hash of its files only and is named in the story. The open tasks of the second lineage are admitted open, each with an executor." ;
    backlog:describesItem ex:Obj3_LinkPassesDone .

ex:Model3_ClassDesign a backlog:ModelArtifact ; rdfs:label "Design of the stored link-pass story, its harness and its evidence"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ClassDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Design ;
    backlog:declaresState "Classes: Story (identifier, title, state, startedAt, finishedAt, lastAuditedAt, executionModality, preLineageItem, admittedByOutput) with associations to AcceptanceCriterion (exactly the criterion of the pass), TestHarness (harnessFor the story, hasHarnessEvidence), TestEvidence (hasTestId, hasTestSpec, hasVerificationMethod, evidenceVerified, verifiedAt) and ArtifactEvidence (hasArtifactPath, hasArtifactSHA256, evidenceVerified, verifiedAt); a StageOutput (hasStateDigest, closedAtCommit) admits the story. A chapter whose check fails has ArtifactEvidence only." ;
    backlog:describesItem ex:Obj3_LinkPassesDone .
ex:ST_Deck_LinkPass backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Data .
ex:ST_Page_LinkPass backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Data .

