ex:CR_SEN0401 a backlog:ClosureReport ; rdfs:label "Closure report of the SEN0401 slides Mission"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:closesForMission ex:Mission ;
    backlog:reportGeneratedAt "2026-10-20T06:57:34"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasClosureSummary "Closure report of the Mission 'Teach SEN0401 from the edition students can now read for free', written 2026-10-20 for the third lineage, after the first two lineages achieved their own scopes. Achieved: for each of the 14 chapters of Mastering Bitcoin 3rd edition the research, the lecture deck and the interactive page are recorded Done with evidence the evidence bridge verified; the supplementary numbers page is Done; the two link passes over all decks and pages are Done; all 45 stories, 99 tasks, the 3 epics and the initiative read Done; all 18 objectives are at target (Obj3_FailuresNamed was corrected forward to 5 on 2026-10-20); the register validates CONFORMANT and every lineage's digests reproduce. NOT achieved or not claimed: (1) The page tests ran against a copy of each page carrying a TEST release key: they prove the page logic, not the instructor's real key. (2) Stand-in pictures remain on the decks named in their audit notes (chapters 2, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13 and 14) where no free picture of the event exists (for example the Bitcoin logo, the Satoshi bust, the Mt. Gox logo, a Trezor Model T for the Safe 5); each note names its slides. (3) Stage4.L, Cross.C, Stage1.C and Stage1.E report NOT_MEASURED (the research files carry no concept inventory) and Cross.B reports CANNOT_RUN (the Stage 3 documents record a section's concept in dcterms:source, not prov:wasDerivedFrom); none of these is a pass and none is claimed as one (08-tooling/stage4_status.md). (4) The page of chapter 8 keeps its known result under the older page test 9.34.0 (113 pass, 1 fail, then a crash); the recorded check runs the newest test 9.35.0 and does not show it; it is unchanged and not claimed to pass. (5) The pages of chapters 8, 10, 11, 12 and 14 are on templates older than 9.51.0 (their page files are v9.51.0, v9.53.0, v9.54.0, v9.55.0 and v9.57.0); the pages of chapters 1 to 7, 9 and 13 are on 9.51.0 (08-tooling/page_jobs_status.md). (6) web.archive.org is unreachable from the build sandbox (the chapter 14 deck links check fails for 1 of 14 links; sec.gov, cnbc.com and coingecko.com also answer 403 or no connection), so those links were not verified by the builders. (7) Stage 4 page ABoxes of the current pipeline exist for chapters 8 to 14 only; the page ABoxes of chapters 1 to 4 and of the numbers page are earlier versions (v9.4.2 and v1.0.0) and chapters 5 to 7 have none. Stage 3.F was repaired for chapters 2 to 4 and 8; the build notes of 2026-10-14 name chapter 7 among those failing it and this register records no repair for it. The register's notes name no gap on chapter 1 or the numbers page, and none is claimed absent. (8) The connectedness findings on 15 research T-Box files (OE v2.18.0 BP-D56 and v2.19.0 BP-D57, shipped after those stories were Done) are not repaired in this lineage: the owner's direction of 2026-10-20 09:19 Istanbul deferred quality and cleaning work, and ruling G133 routes the repair to new work by the change route in a later lineage. This report does not set the Mission outcome or the status of the third lineage; both wait for the owner's act." ;
    backlog:reportsOnObjective ex:Obj2_AdmittedDone, ex:Obj2_DatesFromGit, ex:Obj2_DecksRemaining, ex:Obj2_EvidenceVerified, ex:Obj2_NothingRebuilt, ex:Obj2_PagesRemaining, ex:Obj2_ResearchRemaining, ex:Obj3_DatesFromGit, ex:Obj3_EvidenceVerified, ex:Obj3_FailuresNamed, ex:Obj3_LinkPassesDone, ex:Obj3_NothingRebuilt, ex:Obj3_OpenWorkFinished, ex:Obj_DecksRenewed, ex:Obj_NoUntaughtWork, ex:Obj_PagesBuilt, ex:Obj_ResearchRecorded, ex:Obj_Supplements ;
    backlog:citesFinding ex:Finding_BookChapter4Statements, ex:Finding_BookPrintedResultMismatch, ex:Finding_ChapterAboxTestName, ex:Finding_DecksRevisedFromCourseNotes, ex:Finding_EveryFileVersioned, ex:Finding_ForkedObjectiveTargets, ex:Finding_OwnerMaterials2025Imported, ex:Finding_PageAndCheckToolingForkedAgain, ex:Finding_PageTestConceptTapAndIcons, ex:Finding_PagesOnSharedTemplate942, ex:Finding_PagesRevisedFromCourseNotes, ex:Finding_PagesV3OwnerRules, ex:Finding_RealSoftwareRunAndVerified, ex:Finding_SecondEditionLicence, ex:Finding_Stage4ProposedGatesOnChapter3, ex:Finding_ToolkitCheckedAgainstThree, ex:Finding_WebReaderRefusals, ex:Ruling_Ch03Planned ;
    backlog:statesBestPractice "Read a stage's obligations before writing and satisfy them in the same step; a waiver is drift. The class-model debt of the Backlog stage was paid by a stage revision, not waived." , "Work on the deliverable of a Done story is a story of its own (G125); a task hung under a finished story makes the parent's finish contradict its child." , "Record Done only what the evidence bridge verifies, and never claim a NOT_MEASURED or CANNOT_RUN gate as a pass." , "Count what an objective measures, not the stories that read Done: two readings in this register counted Done stories and were corrected forward." , "Audit status, dates and parent-child agreement before closing: 84 inconsistencies were found in one audit and repaired by sanctioned routes." , "Record work that follows from an owner's direction as owner-directed, with the quoted direction and its time." .

ex:CR_SEN0401 rdfs:comment "Corrected caveat, 2026-10-20 (it replaces the seventh caveat of the summary, which named the gaps from the files and not from a run). Measured on this date with 08-tooling/sen0401_stage4_gates_v1_1_0.py, RDODI's validator unchanged, on main. Chapter 1: Stage3.F FAIL (1 external claim uncited), Stage4.cov FAIL (10 typed individuals lack label and content), Stage4.sub FAIL (116 individuals not substantive). Chapter 2: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov FAIL (10), Stage4.sub FAIL (84). Chapter 3: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov FAIL (10), Stage4.sub FAIL (108). Chapter 4: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov FAIL (10), Stage4.sub FAIL (94). Numbers page: Stage3.F FAIL (19 dangling citations), Stage4.cov FAIL (10), Stage4.sub FAIL (58). Chapters 5, 6 and 7: the Stage 4 runner stops because there is no Stage 4 page ABox, so neither Stage 3.F nor Stage 4 was measured for them in this run; the build notes of 2026-10-14 name chapter 7 among those failing Stage3.F, and no run in this register shows it repaired. In every measured chapter Stage4.L, Cross.C, Stage3.E (concept coverage) are NOT_MEASURED and Cross.B is CANNOT_RUN; none is a pass. Read from the register: the tasks of this lineage on these gates are TK_Research_Ch02_Stage3F, TK_Research_Ch03_Stage3F and TK_Research_Ch04_Stage3F (Stage 3.F of chapters 2 to 4, Done) and the Stage 4 tasks of chapters 8 to 14 (TK_Research_Ch08_Stage4 to TK_Research_Ch14_Stage4, Done). The register holds no task, and no story, for Stage3.F of chapter 1, chapters 5 to 7 or the numbers page, nor for Stage4.cov or Stage4.sub of chapters 1 to 7 or the numbers page: these are not tasks of this lineage. None of the failures listed is claimed as passed; the connectedness agent's status file (branch connectedness-repair) lists the same failures as already on main."@en .

ex:CR3_Gaps a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Close the Stage 3.F and Stage 4 gaps of the chapter materials before the Mission is closed"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR_SEN0401 ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Owner's decision of 2026-10-20 10:42 Istanbul (2026-10-20T07:42:00 UTC), relayed by the coordinator and recorded by the builder session. The question put to him was whether the Mission outcome and the Achieved status of the third lineage are to be recorded now; his answer, quoted: \"No, fill the gaps first.\" That is, the Mission outcome is not recorded now, and the gaps named in the corrected caveat note on the closure report are closed first. The gaps are those of the table in the corrected caveat note of 2026-10-20 on the closure report (v0.121): (1) Stage 3.F of the Stage 3 documents: chapter 1 and Bitcoin in numbers fail; (2) Stage 4: the page ABoxes of chapters 1 to 4 and of Bitcoin in numbers fail Stage4.cov and Stage4.sub and chapters 5, 6 and 7 have none. Stage 3.F of the Stage 3 documents, measured on 2026-10-20 with the lineage chapter check v1_3_0 (Research/ChNN) and the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0: chapter 1 FAIL (1 external claim uncited); Bitcoin in numbers FAIL (19 dangling citations); chapters 2 to 14 PASS (every claim cited, every citation verified; chapters 5, 6 and 7 with 36, 34 and 55 citations, and the whole chapter check PASS for each). The build notes of 2026-10-14 that name chapter 7 as failing, and the stage-4 status note that names chapter 8 (45 dangling citations), are out of date: both chapters pass today. Stage 4 page ABox, measured on 2026-10-20 with the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0: chapters 1, 2, 3, 4 and Bitcoin in numbers have an older ABox that FAILS Stage4.cov (10 typed individuals lack label and content, in each) and Stage4.sub (116, 84, 108, 94 and 58 individuals not substantive); chapters 5, 6 and 7 have no Stage 4 page ABox, so the runner stops with an IndexError; chapters 8 to 14 have one that passes. None of this work is in the scope of the third lineage as it stands: the scope admits the two link passes and the 20 open tasks of the second lineage, and none of those tasks names a Stage 4 ABox of chapters 1 to 7 or the Stage 3.F of chapter 1 or of Bitcoin in numbers. The change grows the scope. It is recorded as Pending and becomes Accepted in the version that records the ScopeChange admitting the stories, because a ScopeChange must name what it admits and the stories exist only when the Backlog stage is rebuilt. Not in this change: the connectedness repair of the T-Box files (deferred by the owner on 2026-10-20 09:19 Istanbul), and any change to a gate, a test or a threshold." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA3_Gaps a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What closing the Stage 3.F and Stage 4 gaps costs, measured before any of it is started"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_Gaps ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR_SEN0401 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "Measured before the work, 2026-10-20: Stage 3.F of the Stage 3 documents, measured on 2026-10-20 with the lineage chapter check v1_3_0 (Research/ChNN) and the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0: chapter 1 FAIL (1 external claim uncited); Bitcoin in numbers FAIL (19 dangling citations); chapters 2 to 14 PASS (every claim cited, every citation verified; chapters 5, 6 and 7 with 36, 34 and 55 citations, and the whole chapter check PASS for each). The build notes of 2026-10-14 that name chapter 7 as failing, and the stage-4 status note that names chapter 8 (45 dangling citations), are out of date: both chapters pass today. Stage 4 page ABox, measured on 2026-10-20 with the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0: chapters 1, 2, 3, 4 and Bitcoin in numbers have an older ABox that FAILS Stage4.cov (10 typed individuals lack label and content, in each) and Stage4.sub (116, 84, 108, 94 and 58 individuals not substantive); chapters 5, 6 and 7 have no Stage 4 page ABox, so the runner stops with an IndexError; chapters 8 to 14 have one that passes. Route (rulings G125, G127, G133): the work has criteria of its own, so it is stories of its own; a deliverable added to a closed scope statement is a revision from the Scope stage, not a scope change alone. What moves: the digests of the Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog stages of the third lineage move once, when the stages are closed again; the first and second lineages are not touched. What does not move: no Done story is re-dated or re-opened, the two link passes and the 20 carried tasks are re-admitted by admission, and the Mission and its stage stand. New work, planned in the Backlog version: two stories, as G133 asks one story with one acceptance criterion per file, and not one story per chapter: the story for Stage 3.F carries 2 criteria (chapter 1, Bitcoin in numbers) and the story for the Stage 4 page ABox 8 criteria (chapters 1 to 7, Bitcoin in numbers), each with its own result; 20 execution tasks (a build and a verify task per unit). Chapters 5, 6 and 7 need no Stage 3.F task: they were measured and pass, which corrects the stale build notes that name chapter 7 as failing. Iteration: the work is planned into a new twelfth iteration of the third lineage, proposed to end at the same time as the eleventh, 2026-10-23T06:00 UTC (Friday 09:00 Istanbul, the end the owner confirmed for the eleventh on 2026-10-19), because the owner wants the lineage finished as soon as possible; the end is the owner's own confirmed end date of the eleventh iteration (accepted for this iteration by the coordinator on 2026-10-20) and the owner may move it. The eleventh iteration was considered and not used: it belongs to the second lineage, which is Achieved, and a container the successor cannot carry (the validator refuses a lineage recorded Achieved while a container of it holds open items, and refuses a wound-down lineage's container left open once the successor's Backlog stage has closed); the successor builds sprints of its own. If a story is still open when the iteration ends, the register shows it as spillover (L4) until the owner rebaselines the iteration or recommits the story; nothing is moved here. Risk: the Stage 4 builder v2.0.0 reads a chapter number and not the unit named numbers, so Bitcoin in numbers may need a new version of the builder (a new tool version is allowed; a gate change is not). Cost of waiting: the Mission outcome and the Achieved status stay unrecorded, as the owner decided. Cost of acting: one change request, one assessment, one stage revision (the retraction and the four rebuilt stages, one commit each), two stories, 20 tasks and a new iteration; enforcement value forgone: none. Nothing is waived and no digest is re-recorded outside the revision." .

ex:Revision_Lineage3_Scope a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Scope stage: the Stage 3.F and Stage 4 gaps are closed before the Mission outcome is recorded"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Scope ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Gaps, ex:IA3_Gaps ;
    backlog:revisionReason "Owner's decision of 2026-10-20 10:42 Istanbul (2026-10-20T07:42:00 UTC), relayed by the coordinator and recorded by the builder session. The question put to him was whether the Mission outcome and the Achieved status of the third lineage are to be recorded now; his answer, quoted: \"No, fill the gaps first.\" That is, the Mission outcome is not recorded now, and the gaps named in the corrected caveat note on the closure report are closed first. The work that closes the gaps adds two deliverables to the scope of the third lineage (the Stage 3.F repair of two Stage 3 documents and the Stage 4 page ABox of eight units); the lineage is in its closed Backlog stage, and a deliverable added to a closed scope statement is a revision from the Scope stage (ruling G127). The change request ex:CR3_Gaps and the impact assessment ex:IA3_Gaps were recorded first, in the previous version. This version retracts the Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog outputs and rebuilds nothing; the outputs are rebuilt one stage and one commit at a time, each consuming the last unretracted output above it; the goals, objectives and stories already in the register re-enter by admission and are not re-dated. The retracted outputs and their digests stay in the register as history (L-112). The interim versions are the declared transition (G129): the items admitted by the retracted Backlog output keep their exemption while the revision is under way. The revision is recorded as decided by the builder role: the owner decided that the gaps are closed first, and the revision is the route that decision needs; the stage revision itself he did not decide." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_Scope, ex:Out3_Goal, ex:Out3_ObjectiveR, ex:Out3_BacklogR ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "a2b0c80" .
ex:Out3_Scope backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_Goal backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_ObjectiveR backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_BacklogR backlog:outputRetracted true .

