    backlog:hasDurationSource "Proposed by the builder session on 2026-10-20 after the owner's direction of 2026-10-20 10:42 Istanbul (2026-10-20T07:42:00 UTC) (quoted in ex:CR3_Gaps): the end is that of the eleventh iteration, Friday 2026-10-23 06:00 UTC (09:00 Istanbul), which the owner confirmed on 2026-10-19; the start is the time of planning. The end is the owner's own confirmed end date (2026-10-19), accepted for this iteration by the coordinator on 2026-10-20; the owner may move it." ;
    backlog:hasSprintGoal "The Stage 3 documents of chapter 1 and Bitcoin in numbers pass Stage 3.F and the Stage 4 page ABox of chapters 1 to 7 and Bitcoin in numbers passes the Stage 4 gate run, each on the gates as they stand, each unit that fails named; then the owner records the Mission outcome." ;
    backlog:hasMember ex:ST_Gap_Stage3F, ex:ST_Gap_Stage4, ex:TK_Gap3F_Ch01_Build, ex:TK_Gap3F_Ch01_Verify, ex:TK_Gap3F_Numbers_Build, ex:TK_Gap3F_Numbers_Verify, ex:TK_GapS4_Ch01_Build, ex:TK_GapS4_Ch01_Verify, ex:TK_GapS4_Ch02_Build, ex:TK_GapS4_Ch02_Verify, ex:TK_GapS4_Ch03_Build, ex:TK_GapS4_Ch03_Verify, ex:TK_GapS4_Ch04_Build, ex:TK_GapS4_Ch04_Verify, ex:TK_GapS4_Ch05_Build, ex:TK_GapS4_Ch05_Verify, ex:TK_GapS4_Ch06_Build, ex:TK_GapS4_Ch06_Verify, ex:TK_GapS4_Ch07_Build, ex:TK_GapS4_Ch07_Verify, ex:TK_GapS4_Numbers_Build, ex:TK_GapS4_Numbers_Verify .
ex:PB3G_Iter_12 a backlog:PlanBaseline ; rdfs:label "Plan baseline of iteration 12 when it was planned"@en ; backlog:baselineFor ex:Iter_12 ; backlog:baselinedAt "2026-10-20T16:04:32"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:isCurrentBaseline true ; backlog:hasBaselineStart "2026-10-20T16:04:32"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasBaselineEnd "2026-10-23T06:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .
ex:Obj3_Stage3FPass backlog:metricMovableBy ex:ST_Gap_Stage3F .
ex:Obj3_Stage4Pass backlog:metricMovableBy ex:ST_Gap_Stage4 .
ex:SC3_Gaps a backlog:ScopeChange ;
    rdfs:label "Scope grown by the Stage 3.F repair and the Stage 4 page ABox of eight units"@en ;
    backlog:fulfillsRequest ex:CR3_Gaps ; backlog:changesScope ex:Scope3 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:admitsItem ex:ST_Gap_Stage3F, ex:ST_Gap_Stage4 ;
    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "Owner's decision of 2026-10-20 10:42 Istanbul (2026-10-20T07:42:00 UTC), relayed by the coordinator and recorded by the builder session. The question put to him was whether the Mission outcome and the Achieved status of the third lineage are to be recorded now; his answer, quoted: \"No, fill the gaps first.\" That is, the Mission outcome is not recorded now, and the gaps named in the corrected caveat note on the closure report are closed first. The boundary moved outward by two stories because the owner decided that the gaps are closed before the Mission outcome is recorded. It is paid for by running the work inside the twelfth iteration, proposed to end with the eleventh (the end the owner confirmed), by building new files beside the old ones, and by leaving every gate, test and threshold as it stands." .
ex:CR3_Gaps rdfs:comment "Disposition set to Accepted on 2026-10-20 in the version that records the ScopeChange ex:SC3_Gaps and the stories it admits; it was Pending in the version that recorded the change request, because a ScopeChange must name what it admits. The owner's decision of 2026-10-20 10:42 Istanbul (2026-10-20T07:42:00 UTC) (quoted above) is the decision."@en .

ex:Out3_BacklogR2 a backlog:StageOutput ;
    rdfs:label "Closure of the Backlog stage of the third lineage, rebuilt by the stage revision from the Scope stage"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:outputOfStage backlog:Stage_Backlog ;
    backlog:consumesOutput ex:Out3_ObjectiveR2 ;
    backlog:hasStateDigest "8c2e79fb4daef421af1a7923f93a7936546a20d5a800a74b8101e30d52e16f0f" ;
    backlog:closedAtCommit "e7ede29" .

ex:CR3_Gaps5 a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Close the Stage 3.F gap of chapter 5, found by measurement after the gaps were planned"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Gaps, ex:SC3_Gaps ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Owner's decision of 2026-10-20 10:42 Istanbul (2026-10-20T07:42:00 UTC), relayed by the coordinator and recorded by the builder session. His direction, quoted: \"No, fill the gaps first.\", covers every gap in the Stage 3.F and Stage 4 table; this gap was not in the table because it was found by measurement afterwards. Found by measurement later, not hidden: on 2026-10-20 (after the work on the other units had begun) the coordinator ran the Stage 4 gate runner for chapter 5 and Stage3.F reported 15 dangling citations; the lineage chapter check (08-tooling/sen0401_lineage_chapter_check_v1_3_0.py) passes the same document because it reads the pinned validator of the ecosystem checkout (v1.6.0), while the Stage 4 runner reads the current validator (rdodi_pipeline_validator_v1_13_0). My earlier statement that Stage 3.F passes for chapters 2 to 14 was measured with the pinned validator. Re-measured with the current validator on 2026-10-20: chapters 1 to 4, 6 to 14 and Bitcoin in numbers pass (chapter 1 and Bitcoin in numbers after their repair); chapter 5 fails. The deliverable ex:Del3_Stage3FRepair is the Stage 3 documents that fail Stage 3.F passing it; its text names the two units measured then, so chapter 5 widens it by one unit. A ScopeDeliverable's subject is the same, so the Scope digest does not move; the new acceptance criterion is counted by the Backlog digest, so the route is a revision from the Backlog stage (G125 route 2), not from the Scope stage. Pending until the ScopeChange that admits the story's new criterion and tasks is recorded." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA3_Gaps5 a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What closing the Stage 3.F gap of chapter 5 costs, measured before it is started"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_Gaps5 ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Gaps ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "Measured 2026-10-20: Found by measurement later, not hidden: on 2026-10-20 (after the work on the other units had begun) the coordinator ran the Stage 4 gate runner for chapter 5 and Stage3.F reported 15 dangling citations; the lineage chapter check (08-tooling/sen0401_lineage_chapter_check_v1_3_0.py) passes the same document because it reads the pinned validator of the ecosystem checkout (v1.6.0), while the Stage 4 runner reads the current validator (rdodi_pipeline_validator_v1_13_0). My earlier statement that Stage 3.F passes for chapters 2 to 14 was measured with the pinned validator. Re-measured with the current validator on 2026-10-20: chapters 1 to 4, 6 to 14 and Bitcoin in numbers pass (chapter 1 and Bitcoin in numbers after their repair); chapter 5 fails. What moves: the Backlog digest of the third lineage, once, when the stage is closed again by a revision from the Backlog stage (one more criterion, AC3G_3F_Ch05); the Scope, Goal and Objective digests do not move. New items: one criterion on the open story ex:ST_Gap_Stage3F, a Build and a Verify task for chapter 5 (planned into the same iteration, ex:Iter_12, ending 2026-10-23T06:00 UTC, the owner's own confirmed end date). The target of the objective ex:Obj3_Stage3FPass moves from 2 to 3 documents (a state, not a stage element; disclosed on it). No Done story is re-dated; the 10 started Build tasks and their stories keep their states and start times; the carried items are re-admitted by admission. Interim: while the Backlog output is retracted the register shows the declared interim violations (G129). Nothing is waived, no gate, test or threshold is changed (the validator difference is disclosed, not repaired). Cost of waiting: the Mission outcome stays unrecorded and a document that fails the gate the runner uses stays unrepaired. Cost of acting: three commits and about half an hour; enforcement value forgone: none." .

ex:Revision_Lineage3_Backlog5 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Backlog stage: the Stage 3.F gap of chapter 5"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Backlog ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Gaps5, ex:IA3_Gaps5 ;
    backlog:revisionReason "Owner's decision of 2026-10-20 10:42 Istanbul (2026-10-20T07:42:00 UTC), relayed by the coordinator and recorded by the builder session. His direction, quoted: \"No, fill the gaps first.\", covers every gap in the Stage 3.F and Stage 4 table; this gap was not in the table because it was found by measurement afterwards. Found by measurement later, not hidden: on 2026-10-20 (after the work on the other units had begun) the coordinator ran the Stage 4 gate runner for chapter 5 and Stage3.F reported 15 dangling citations; the lineage chapter check (08-tooling/sen0401_lineage_chapter_check_v1_3_0.py) passes the same document because it reads the pinned validator of the ecosystem checkout (v1.6.0), while the Stage 4 runner reads the current validator (rdodi_pipeline_validator_v1_13_0). My earlier statement that Stage 3.F passes for chapters 2 to 14 was measured with the pinned validator. Re-measured with the current validator on 2026-10-20: chapters 1 to 4, 6 to 14 and Bitcoin in numbers pass (chapter 1 and Bitcoin in numbers after their repair); chapter 5 fails. The new acceptance criterion of the open story ex:ST_Gap_Stage3F is counted by the Backlog digest, so the Backlog stage is revised (G125 route 2): this version retracts the Backlog output ex:Out3_BacklogR2 and rebuilds nothing; the next version rebuilds it, re-admitting the same items by admission, not re-dated. The change request ex:CR3_Gaps5 and the impact assessment ex:IA3_Gaps5 are in the previous version. The interim version is the declared transition (G129). Recorded as decided by the builder role: the owner decided that every gap is filled first; the revision is the route that needs." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR2 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "e6ba421" .
ex:Out3_BacklogR2 backlog:outputRetracted true .


ex:AC3G_3F_Ch05 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "Stage 3.F passes for the Stage 3 document of chapter 5"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given the Stage 3 document of chapter 5 and its research data, when the Stage 3.F gate is run on them by the lineage chapter check for Research/Ch05 and by the Stage 4 gate runner for ch05, then Stage3.F reports PASS (measured on 2026-10-20: FAIL, FAIL, 15 dangling citations under the current validator that the Stage 4 gate runner uses; the chapter check, which reads the pinned validator, passes) with no gate, test or threshold changed and no citation or claim removed only to pass; if it still reports FAIL the unit is named failing and this criterion has no passing result." ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the Stage3.F line of the Stage 4 gate runner (current validator) and of the chapter check, verified by the evidence bridge, and the new research and document data cited by SHA-256" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC3G_3F_Passes, ex:TC3G_3F_NotClaimed .
ex:TC3G_3F_Passes backlog:exercisesCriterion ex:AC3G_3F_Ch05 .
ex:TC3G_3F_NotClaimed backlog:exercisesCriterion ex:AC3G_3F_Ch05 .

